- U>W | help a younger child who is working for the same badge | v: benevolence | chance: 76
- B>U | talk the grown-ups into lessons with the best teacher around | door | v: achievement, power | chance: 58
- R>B | show it off to the ones who laughed at you, and gloat | v: power | mark: made an enemy | act: show it off to the ones who laughed at them, and gloat | chance: 42
- G>R | spend the rest of the summer outdoors, with no lessons at all | door | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 65
works: The certificate goes up on the fridge, and {N} stops to look at it every morning.
works: {N} moves up to the next class with the older ones, a little taller than before.
fails: Half the class got the same badge, and nobody seems very impressed.
fails: The day goes sour when {sibling} sulks about it, and {N} wonders what all the practice was for.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: money worries end (cycle s1)

== money worries end
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
per_year: 0 0 .018 .024 .03 .018
drivers: prosper+.4 money+.4 health+.2 stress-.3 unrest-.3 fortune+.1
gap: 3-8
times: repeats: about 3 in 100 young adults, 4 in 100 adults, 5 in 100 people in midlife and 3 in 100 elders a year see their money worries end: the last debt cleared, or a secure income at last (D18 [est]), leaning on household debt cycles: debts peak in the thirties and forties and fall with age, and pensions begin in old age. Point 12 (Emren 2026-10-05): the yearly figures above are lowered to 0, 0, .018, .024, .03, .018 (child to elder): only after money worries (the engine is asked for that gate).
likelier: a growing economy, a steady income, a promotion or a legacy that clears the debt, good health
rarer: low money, poor health, stress, unrest, a divorce
tone: joy
life: money, home
horizon: months
roles: partner, parent, friend, child, sibling
earth: the last payment goes through: the debt is cleared, and the money will be there next month too
scene: The last payment goes through on an ordinary Tuesday. {N} looks at the screen for a long time: nothing owed, and next month's money already promised.
scene W: {N} crosses the final line off the list on the fridge, the list {N} has kept for six years, payment by payment.
scene U: {N} opens the spreadsheet one last time and watches the line of debt touch zero.
scene B: Nobody holds anything over {N} now: not the bank, not the card company, not {parent}.
scene R: {N} walks out of the bank into the sunshine, feeling light enough to float.
scene G: That night {N} sleeps straight through until morning, the way {N} slept as a child.
- W | pay back the friend who lent to you in the worst year, to the last penny | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: kept your word | act: pay back the friend who lent to them in the worst year, to the last penny | chance: 76
- U | study money properly, so it never happens again | v: self-direction, security | mark: learned a skill | chance: 72
- B | buy yourself the expensive thing you were refused all those years | v: hedonism, power | chance: 64
- R | quit the job you only kept for the debts | door | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 62
- G | keep every spare penny inside the family, and turn away the friend who asks | v: security, tradition | mark: refused someone in need | closed: approval: refusing the friend who stood by them; backfire: the friendship sours, and word gets round | chance: 75
- W>U | sit down with an adviser and draw up a proper plan for the years ahead | v: security | tags: win:money+.05 | chance: 74
- U>B | work out how to make the spare money earn more money | v: achievement, power | tags: win:money+.05 | chance: 65
- B>R | take out a new loan at once for the motorbike or the trip you always wanted | binds | v: hedonism, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | tags: pay:money-.1 | chance: 32
- R>G | throw a big dinner for everyone who saw you through the lean years | v: benevolence, hedonism | tags: pay:money-.05 | act: throw a big dinner for everyone who saw them through the lean years | chance: 80
- G>W | go back to the family's old way: a jar for every bill, and cash only | habit | v: tradition, security | tags: win:money+.05 | chance: 78
works: {N} stops checking the bank balance every morning, and the habit does not come back.
works: A year later {N} has savings for the first time, a small cushion that grows a little every month.
fails: Within a year the old debts have found new ways to come back.
fails: {N} keeps waking at four to worry, even with nothing left to worry about.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a stranger saves you, or you save one (cycle s3)
# Audit 2026-10-05: split at 12. This version is for 12 and over; "a stranger to the rescue" (variant_of) is the child's.

== a stranger saves you, or you save one
tier: life event
stages: all
age: 12-95
per_year: .01 .01 .01 .01 .01 .015
drivers: harsh+.3 unrest+.2 community+.2 ties+.2 era-.2
gap: 5-15
times: repeats: about 5 in 1,000 children, 1 in 100 people from the teenage years to midlife, and 1.5 in 100 elders a year are saved by a stranger, or save one: pulled from water, helped at a roadside, brought round in the street (D36 [est]); a close call that ends without a stranger comes as a narrow escape; under 12 the event comes as "a stranger to the rescue", which carries the child rate (audit 2026-10-05)
likelier: a harsh place with real dangers, unrest, a close community and wide ties that put people in each other's way
rarer: a sheltered and private life, an era in which people meet fewer strangers
tone: mixed
life: community, body
horizon: moment
roles: friend, partner, parent, child, a stranger
earth: at the lake one stranger goes under and another pulls them out, and one of the two is you
scene: Ten minutes ago they had never met. Now two strangers sit on the shore of the lake, soaked and shaking under one foil blanket, and one of them owes the other a life. One of them is {N}.
scene W: There will be a statement for the police, perhaps a letter from the council. {N} is already thinking about what is owed now, and to whom.
scene U: {N} keeps replaying it: the cold, the weeds, the half second when it could have gone either way.
scene B: A crowd has gathered and someone is filming. Even now, {N} notices that.
scene R: {Ns} heart is still hammering. {N} grips the stranger's hand and will not let go.
scene G: The lake is flat and quiet again, as if nothing happened. {N} watches it and feels very small and very alive.
- W | visit the stranger's family with a proper gift, and keep in touch every year | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: made a friend | chance: 59
- U | go back to the spot and work out exactly what went wrong | v: self-direction, security | chance: 61
- B | sell the story and the video to whoever pays most | v: power, achievement | chance: 48
- R | hug the stranger and cry, right there on the shore | v: none clear (relief let out) | chance: 90
- G | take it as a sign that you were meant to be there, that day | identity | v: none clear (a sense of fate) | chance: 72
- W>R | join the lifesaving club, with its drills and rotas, to be ready next time | door | v: benevolence, stimulation | chance: 65
- U>G | learn the stranger's whole story, and find out how your lives connect | door | v: self-direction, universalism | mark: made a friend | chance: 50
- B>W | use all the attention to push the council for a rail and a lifebuoy | v: universalism, power | chance: 68
- R>U | go back into the water the very next day, to master the fear | body: heavy | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 68
- G>B | treat the stranger as kin from now on, and expect kin's loyalty back | binds | v: power, tradition | mark: made a friend | chance: 42
works: {N} and the stranger stay in touch for years, two lives tied together by one afternoon.
works: The fear fades, and what stays is a strange, bright gratitude.
fails: {N} dreams about the water for months.
fails: The stranger walks off without a word, and {N} never learns their name.

