age: 12-95
per_year: 0 .006 .006 .004 .004 .002
drivers: era+.4 community+.2 stress+.2 ties-.3 trouble+.1
gap: 5-15
times: repeats: about 3 in 100 teenagers and young adults, 2 in 100 adults and people in midlife, and 1 in 100 elders a year are shamed in public for something they really said or did (D83 [est], set lower than its youth figures, which lean on peer rejection; being cast out by peers is a separate thing); an untrue rumour comes as an outside event, and an old hidden wrong as an echo. Point 12 (Emren 2026-10-05): the yearly figures above are lowered to 0, .006, .006, .004, .004, .002 (child to elder): about 1 in 3 people are shamed in public at some point (estimate); the old rate gave two a life.
